<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry XIII, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1235">1235</a>–1290</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry I of Lower Bavaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry XIII, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, was a Wittelsbach prince who received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> as his seat, when he and his brother Louis II the Strict divided the duchy in 1255. The partition began the long series of Wittelsbach divisions of Bavaria. His son Otto III was briefly King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-xiii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Henry XIII, Duke of Bavaria" width="313" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonym - cca 1310 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_XIII._(Bayern).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
